---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Boing Network"
  description="Boing is an independent Layer 1 where quality is enforced by the protocol, with transparent deployment checks and open participation for users, developers and validators. Public testnet; mainnet not live."
  canonical="/"
>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="hero" id="hero">
    <div class="hero-grid" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="hero-content">
      <span class="stage-badge">Public testnet &mdash; mainnet not live</span>
      <img src="/logo.svg" alt="Boing Network" class="hero-logo-img" width="96" height="96" />
      <h1 class="hero-title font-display">Quality, enforced by the protocol.</h1>
      <p class="hero-brandline">Boing Network &mdash; the quality-assured Layer 1</p>
      <p class="tagline">Boing is an independent Layer 1 built from first principles, with transparent deployment checks and open participation for users, developers and validators.</p>
      <div class="cta">
        <a href="/testnet" class="btn btn-primary">Explore the testnet</a>
        <a href="/developers/quickstart" class="btn btn-secondary">Build on Boing</a>
        <a href="/testnet/join" class="btn btn-outline">Run a node</a>
      </div>
      <ul class="proof-chips" aria-label="Proof points">
        <li>Public testnet and faucet</li>
        <li>Purpose-built VM, not EVM-compatible</li>
        <li>~2-second target block time under load</li>
        <li>Open validator and node participation</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The problem -->
  <section class="section" id="problem">
    <h2 class="section-reveal">Blockchains make it easy to deploy. Boing adds a quality gate.</h2>
    <p class="section-lead section-reveal delay-1">The Boing Quality Gate screens deployments against transparent rules before they reach the ledger. Automated checks handle clear cases; a decentralized community pool reviews edge cases.</p>
    <div class="problem-grid">
      <div class="info-card section-reveal delay-2">
        <h3>What it is</h3>
        <p>Boing introduces protocol-level deployment checks designed to identify and restrict deployments that fail transparent quality criteria before they are accepted on-chain.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="info-card section-reveal delay-3">
        <h3>What it is designed to do</h3>
        <p>Designed to reduce malicious, deceptive and low-quality deployments through transparent, protocol-level checks. The rules are public, and outcomes remain visible.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="info-card section-reveal delay-4">
        <h3>What it does not claim</h3>
        <p>No gate can prevent every kind of abuse. The Quality Gate reduces risk and makes decisions auditable; it does not replace your own review of an application. <a href="/pdfs/QUALITY-ASSURANCE-NETWORK.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read the QA design (PDF)</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- How it works -->
  <section class="section section-alt" id="how">
    <h2 class="section-reveal">How the Quality Gate works</h2>
    <p class="section-lead section-reveal delay-1">Five steps from submission to a public, auditable outcome.</p>
    <ol class="gate-steps">
      <li class="section-reveal delay-2"><span class="gate-num">1</span><div><h3>Deployment submitted</h3><p>A developer submits contract bytecode with a declared purpose.</p></div></li>
      <li class="section-reveal delay-3"><span class="gate-num">2</span><div><h3>Automated checks evaluate it</h3><p>Transparent rules cover bytecode, size, opcodes and declared purpose.</p></div></li>
      <li class="section-reveal delay-4"><span class="gate-num">3</span><div><h3>Clear cases are decided by the protocol</h3><p>Deployments that clearly meet or clearly fail the rules are accepted or rejected, with the rule that applied.</p></div></li>
      <li class="section-reveal delay-5"><span class="gate-num">4</span><div><h3>Edge cases go to the community pool</h3><p>When the rules cannot decide, a decentralized pool of reviewers does.</p></div></li>
      <li class="section-reveal delay-6"><span class="gate-num">5</span><div><h3>Outcomes remain visible and auditable</h3><p>Decisions are observable in <a href="https://boing.observer/qa" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Boing Observer</a>, not hidden in a private process.</p></div></li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <!-- Built from first principles -->
  <section class="section" id="principles">
    <h2 class="section-reveal">Built from first principles</h2>
    <p class="section-lead section-reveal delay-1">An independent chain with its own stack, not a fork or an EVM-compatibility layer.</p>
    <div class="spec-grid">
      <div class="spec section-reveal delay-2"><strong>Rust</strong><span>Protocol and node implementation</span></div>
      <div class="spec section-reveal delay-2"><strong>HotStuff PoS</strong><span>Proof-of-stake consensus</span></div>
      <div class="spec section-reveal delay-3"><strong>Ed25519</strong><span>Signatures</span></div>
      <div class="spec section-reveal delay-3"><strong>BLAKE3</strong><span>Hashing</span></div>
      <div class="spec section-reveal delay-4"><strong>Purpose-built VM</strong><span>Not EVM-compatible</span></div>
      <div class="spec section-reveal delay-4"><strong>~2 s blocks</strong><span>Target block time when transactions are pending</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="grid pillars-secondary">
      <div class="card section-reveal delay-5"><h3>Secure by design</h3><p>Rust, HotStuff proof of stake, Ed25519 and BLAKE3.</p></div>
      <div class="card section-reveal delay-6"><h3>Open participation</h3><p>Permissionless for users, developers and validators.</p></div>
      <div class="card section-reveal delay-7"><h3>Transparent by default</h3><p>Observable rules, deployments and outcomes.</p></div>
      <div class="card section-reveal delay-8"><h3>Built for real applications</h3><p>Native accounts, adaptive gas and cross-chain liquidity.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Choose your role -->
  <section class="section section-alt" id="roles">
    <h2 class="section-reveal">Choose your role</h2>
    <p class="section-lead section-reveal delay-1">Start where you are. Everything below runs on the public testnet.</p>
    <div class="roles-grid">
      <article class="role-card section-reveal delay-2">
        <h3>Use the network</h3>
        <p class="role-line">A safer way to explore on-chain applications.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Create a wallet with Boing Express</li>
          <li>Get testnet BOING from the faucet</li>
          <li>Send and receive</li>
          <li>Explore accounts, blocks and transactions in Boing Observer</li>
          <li>Connect to applications</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="role-links"><a href="https://boing.express" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Boing Express</a><a href="/faucet">Faucet</a><a href="https://boing.observer" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Boing Observer</a></div>
      </article>
      <article class="role-card section-reveal delay-3">
        <h3>Build an application</h3>
        <p class="role-line">Build on an independent chain with native account and application primitives.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>JSON-RPC and the Boing SDK</li>
          <li>Purpose-built VM</li>
          <li>Native account abstraction, session keys and social recovery</li>
          <li>Adaptive gas</li>
          <li>Deployment QA requirements</li>
          <li>Clear testnet docs</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="role-links"><a href="/developers/quickstart">Quickstart</a><a href="/docs/rpc-api">RPC API</a><a href="/docs">Docs</a></div>
      </article>
      <article class="role-card section-reveal delay-4">
        <h3>Run a node</h3>
        <p class="role-line">Help operate an open network with transparent participation rules.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Rust node with HotStuff consensus</li>
          <li>Public testnet and node setup guides</li>
          <li>Validator registration</li>
          <li>Slashing and appeals rules</li>
          <li>Launch-partner pathway</li>
          <li>Mainnet readiness milestones</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="role-links"><a href="/testnet/join">Run a node</a><a href="/testnet/operators">Operators</a><a href="/bootnodes">Bootnodes</a></div>
      </article>
    </div>
    <p class="institution-note section-reveal delay-5">For institutions: Boing is designed for verifiability and institutional review, with transparent, rule-based infrastructure for applications that require verifiable deployment standards. Audits, genesis, incident response and mainnet readiness are still open items; see the roadmap below.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- Honest roadmap -->
  <section class="section" id="roadmap">
    <h2 class="section-reveal">Honest roadmap</h2>
    <p class="section-lead section-reveal delay-1">Testnet status is a strength: here is what exists, what is being built, and what must be true before mainnet.</p>
    <div class="road-grid">
      <div class="road-col section-reveal delay-2">
        <span class="road-tag road-live">Live on testnet</span>
        <ul>
          <li>Public testnet RPC and faucet</li>
          <li>Quality Gate deployment checks, with a published rule registry</li>
          <li>Boing Express wallet (web and Chrome extension)</li>
          <li>Boing Observer explorer, including QA visibility</li>
          <li>Node, CLI and SDK tooling</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="road-col section-reveal delay-3">
        <span class="road-tag road-dev">In development</span>
        <ul>
          <li>Community review pool for edge cases</li>
          <li>Validator set growth and production hardening</li>
          <li>Cross-chain liquidity routes in Boing Finance</li>
          <li>Incentivized testnet programme</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="road-col section-reveal delay-4">
        <span class="road-tag road-req">Required before mainnet</span>
        <ul>
          <li>Independent security audits</li>
          <li>Genesis and launch-partner validator readiness</li>
          <li>Finalized slashing and appeals process</li>
          <li>Incident-response process</li>
          <li>Published mainnet readiness milestones met</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="road-col section-reveal delay-5">
        <span class="road-tag road-no">Not yet complete</span>
        <ul>
          <li>Mainnet: not live</li>
          <li>Independent audits: not complete</li>
          <li>Institutional review materials</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Ecosystem -->
  <section class="section section-alt" id="ecosystem">
    <h2 class="section-reveal">The Boing ecosystem</h2>
    <p class="section-lead section-reveal delay-1">Four products, one network. Start on the public testnet in three steps.</p>
    <ol class="first-steps section-reveal delay-2" aria-label="First steps on the Boing testnet">
      <li><a href="https://boing.express" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>1. Get a wallet</strong><span>Create a Boing Express wallet (web or Chrome extension).</span></a></li>
      <li><a href="/faucet"><strong>2. Get testnet BOING</strong><span>Request free testnet BOING for fees.</span></a></li>
      <li><a href="https://boing.observer" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>3. Send and verify</strong><span>Send your first transaction, then find it in Boing Observer.</span></a></li>
    </ol>
    <div class="apps-row">
      <a href="/docs/getting-started" class="app-card section-reveal delay-3">
        <h3>Boing Network</h3>
        <p class="app-tag">The quality-assured Layer 1</p>
        <p>The core protocol and ecosystem: docs, faucet, node setup and the Quality Gate.</p>
        <span class="app-status live">Public testnet</span>
      </a>
      <a href="https://boing.express" class="app-card section-reveal delay-4" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        <h3>Boing Express</h3>
        <p class="app-tag">Your gateway to Boing</p>
        <p>A non-custodial wallet designed for the Boing ecosystem, for the web and Chrome.</p>
        <span class="app-status live">Public testnet</span>
      </a>
      <a href="https://boing.observer" class="app-card section-reveal delay-5" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        <h3>Boing Observer</h3>
        <p class="app-tag">See what happens on-chain</p>
        <p>An explorer with integrated QA transparency: blocks, transactions, accounts and Quality Gate decisions.</p>
        <span class="app-status live">Public testnet</span>
      </a>
      <a href="https://boing.finance" class="app-card section-reveal delay-6" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        <h3>Boing Finance</h3>
        <p class="app-tag">Move liquidity across chains</p>
        <p>A cross-chain liquidity interface spanning Boing and external networks.</p>
        <span class="app-status build">Evolving</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- Tokenomics -->
  <section class="section section-alt" id="tokenomics">
    <h2 class="section-reveal">Tokenomics</h2>
    <p class="section-lead section-reveal delay-1">Sustainable value design — <strong>uncapped total supply</strong> with a <strong>set initial supply</strong> at mainnet launch. When circulating supply reaches the floor, new waves are minted to rebalance.</p>
    <div class="stats-grid">
      <div class="stat-card section-reveal delay-2"><span class="stat-value">Uncapped</span><span class="stat-label">Total Supply</span></div>
      <div class="stat-card section-reveal delay-3"><span class="stat-value">Set at launch</span><span class="stat-label">Initial Supply</span></div>
      <div class="stat-card section-reveal delay-4"><span class="stat-value">~2s</span><span class="stat-label">Target Block Time (when transactions are pending)</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="chart-card chart-fullwidth section-reveal delay-5">
      <h3>Initial Supply Allocation</h3>
      <p class="chart-intro">How the fixed initial supply (at mainnet launch) is allocated. Staking rewards are topped up by new waves when supply reaches the floor, so the initial allocation leans more toward treasury and community.</p>
      <div class="chart-wrapper chart-supply chart-pie-wrap">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" class="supply-pie-svg">
          <circle cx="50" cy="50" r="40" fill="none" class="stroke-teal" stroke-width="40" stroke-dasharray="138.2 113.1" stroke-dashoffset="0" transform="rotate(-90 50 50)" stroke-linecap="butt" />
          <circle cx="50" cy="50" r="40" fill="none" class="stroke-cyan" stroke-width="40" stroke-dasharray="75.4 175.9" stroke-dashoffset="-138.2" transform="rotate(-90 50 50)" stroke-linecap="butt" />
          <circle cx="50" cy="50" r="40" fill="none" class="stroke-success" stroke-width="40" stroke-dasharray="37.7 213.6" stroke-dashoffset="-213.6" transform="rotate(-90 50 50)" stroke-linecap="butt" />
        </svg>
      </div>
      <ul class="legend legend-inline">
        <li><span class="dot dot-teal"></span> Staking Rewards 55%</li>
        <li><span class="dot dot-cyan"></span> Treasury 30%</li>
        <li><span class="dot dot-success"></span> Community & Grants 15%</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="chart-note">Total supply is uncapped. Initial supply is fixed at mainnet launch; new waves mint when circulating supply reaches the floor.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="charts-row">
      <div class="chart-card section-reveal delay-6">
        <h3>Fee Allocation</h3>
        <div class="chart-wrapper chart-doughnut">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" class="doughnut-svg">
            <circle cx="50" cy="50" r="40" fill="none" class="stroke-teal" stroke-width="20" stroke-dasharray="201 50.3" stroke-dashoffset="0" transform="rotate(-90 50 50)" />
            <circle cx="50" cy="50" r="40" fill="none" class="stroke-cyan" stroke-width="20" stroke-dasharray="50.3 201" stroke-dashoffset="-201" transform="rotate(-90 50 50)" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <ul class="legend">
          <li><span class="dot dot-teal"></span> Validators 80%</li>
          <li><span class="dot dot-cyan"></span> Treasury 20%</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="chart-card section-reveal delay-7">
        <h3>Emission Schedule</h3>
        <div class="chart-wrapper chart-line">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 200 120" class="line-svg" preserveAspectRatio="none">
            <defs>
              <linearGradient id="emissionGrad" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1">
                <stop offset="0%" stop-color="var(--accent-teal)" stop-opacity="0.3" />
                <stop offset="100%" stop-color="var(--accent-teal)" stop-opacity="0" />
              </linearGradient>
            </defs>
            <polyline points="0,24 33,48 67,66 100,79 133,90 200,108 200,120 0,120" fill="url(#emissionGrad)" stroke="none" />
            <polyline points="0,24 33,48 67,66 100,79 133,90 200,108" fill="none" class="stroke-teal" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
          </svg>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="value-loop section-reveal delay-8"><strong>Usage ↑</strong> → Fees ↑ → Validators & Treasury ↑ → Security & Ecosystem ↑ → <strong>Value ↑</strong></p>
  </section>
  <!-- Build & Resources (merged: innovations, testnet CTA, CTA banner, resources) -->
  <section class="section" id="build">
    <h2 class="section-reveal">Built for real applications</h2>
    <p class="section-lead section-reveal delay-1">Native accounts, adaptive gas and cross-chain liquidity as supporting capabilities.</p>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card section-reveal delay-2"><h3>Native Account Abstraction</h3><p>Gasless txs, social recovery, session keys — built into the protocol.</p></div>
      <div class="card section-reveal delay-3"><h3>Adaptive Gas Model</h3><p>Dynamic gas that responds to network conditions with predictable caps.</p></div>
      <div class="card section-reveal delay-4"><h3>Cross-chain liquidity</h3><p>Protocol-level primitives for liquidity routing across chains.</p></div>
      <div class="card section-reveal delay-5"><h3>Transparent Slashing</h3><p>Auditable slashing conditions and appeal mechanisms.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="build-banners-row">
      <div class="testnet-banner section-reveal delay-6">
        <h3>Join the testnet</h3>
        <p>Run a node, get testnet BOING from the faucet, and help secure the network. Single node for local dev or multi-node to join the public testnet.</p>
        <div class="testnet-banner-btns">
          <a href="/testnet/join" class="btn btn-testnet">Join Testnet</a>
          <a href="/faucet" class="btn btn-secondary">Get testnet BOING</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="cta-banner section-reveal delay-7">
        <h3>Build on Boing</h3>
        <p>An independent Layer 1 with native account abstraction, adaptive gas and transparent deployment checks. Public testnet; mainnet not live.</p>
        <div class="cta-banner-links">
          <a href="/testnet/join">Join Testnet</a>
          <span class="sep">•</span>
          <a href="/docs/getting-started">Get Started</a>
          <span class="sep">•</span>
          <a href="/developers/quickstart">Developers</a>
          <span class="sep">•</span>
          <a href="https://boing.finance" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Boing Finance</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <h2 class="section-subtitle section-reveal delay-8">Resources</h2>
    <div class="link-grid">
      <a href="/testnet" class="link-highlight link-3d">Dashboard</a>
      <a href="/resources" class="link-highlight link-3d">Resources</a>
      <a href="/testnet/join" class="link-highlight link-3d">Join Testnet</a>
      <a href="/faucet" class="link-3d">Faucet</a>
      <a href="/docs/getting-started" class="link-3d">Getting Started</a>
      <a href="/docs/rpc-api" class="link-3d">RPC API</a>
      <a href="/developers/quickstart" class="link-3d">Developer Quickstart</a>
      <a href="/status" class="link-3d">Network Status</a>
      <a href="/about" class="link-3d">About</a>
      <a href="/community" class="link-3d">Community</a>
    </div>
    <footer class="section-footer">
      <p>Boing Network — Quality, enforced by the protocol. <strong>Public testnet — mainnet not live.</strong></p>
      <div class="footer-links">
        <a href="/testnet">Dashboard</a>
        <a href="/resources">Resources</a>
        <a href="/testnet/join">Join Testnet</a>
        <a href="/faucet">Faucet</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/Boing-Network/boing.network" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
        <a href="https://discord.gg/K3w9nbUw4N" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Discord</a>
        <a href="https://boing.finance" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Boing Finance</a>
        <a href="/docs">Documentation</a>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  /* Boing rebrand: hero, Quality Gate sections, roles, roadmap. Tokens: BRAND.md */
  .hero { position: relative; text-align: center; padding: 5rem 1.5rem 4rem; overflow: hidden; display: grid; place-items: center; min-height: 85vh; background: radial-gradient(ellipse at 50% 30%, rgba(var(--boing-accent-rgb), 0.14), transparent 60%); }
  @media (max-width: 480px) { .hero { padding: 3rem 1rem; min-height: 80vh; } }
  .hero-grid { position: absolute; inset: 0; pointer-events: none; background-image: linear-gradient(rgba(var(--boing-accent-rgb), 0.08) 1px, transparent 1px), linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(var(--boing-accent-rgb), 0.08) 1px, transparent 1px); background-size: 48px 48px; -webkit-mask-image: radial-gradient(ellipse at 50% 40%, #000 15%, transparent 72%); mask-image: radial-gradient(ellipse at 50% 40%, #000 15%, transparent 72%); }
  .hero-content { position: relative; z-index: 1; max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .hero-title { font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 5.5vw, 3.75rem); line-height: 1.1; font-weight: 800; margin: 0.5rem 0 0.75rem; color: var(--boing-text); letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  .hero-brandline { margin: 0 0 1rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.04em; text-transform: uppercase; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--boing-accent-soft); }
  .hero .tagline { font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 2.2vw, 1.3rem); color: var(--text-secondary); max-width: 40rem; margin: 0 auto 1.75rem; line-height: 1.55; }
  .hero .stage-badge { display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 1rem; padding: 0.3rem 0.8rem; border-radius: 999px; font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--boing-warning); border: 1px solid rgba(251, 191, 36, 0.45); background: rgba(251, 191, 36, 0.08); }
  .hero .btn-primary { background: var(--boing-accent); color: var(--boing-accent-ink); }
  .hero .btn-primary:hover { background: var(--boing-accent-soft); filter: none; }
  .proof-chips { list-style: none; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center; gap: 0.5rem 0.75rem; padding: 0; margin: 2rem 0 0; }
  .proof-chips li { padding: 0.35rem 0.8rem; border-radius: 999px; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-secondary); border: 1px solid var(--boing-line); background: rgba(16, 26, 56, 0.6); }
  .problem-grid, .roles-grid, .road-grid { display: grid; gap: 1.25rem; }
  .problem-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr)); }
  .roles-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr)); }
  .road-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr)); }
  .info-card, .role-card, .road-col { background: rgba(16, 26, 56, 0.88); border: 1px solid var(--boing-line); border-radius: 1rem; padding: 1.35rem; }
  .info-card h3, .role-card h3 { margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--text-primary); }
  .info-card p, .role-card li, .road-col li { color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  .info-card p { margin: 0; }
  .info-card a, .role-links a { color: var(--boing-accent-soft); }
  .gate-steps { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0 auto; max-width: 760px; display: grid; gap: 0.9rem; counter-reset: gate; }
  .gate-steps li { display: flex; gap: 1rem; align-items: flex-start; padding: 1rem 1.25rem; border: 1px solid var(--boing-line); border-left: 3px solid var(--boing-accent); border-radius: 0.75rem; background: rgba(16, 26, 56, 0.88); }
  .gate-num { flex: none; width: 2rem; height: 2rem; border-radius: 50%; display: grid; place-items: center; font-weight: 700; color: var(--boing-accent-ink); background: var(--boing-accent); }
  .gate-steps h3 { margin: 0 0 0.2rem; font-size: 1rem; color: var(--text-primary); }
  .gate-steps p { margin: 0; font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-secondary); }
  .gate-steps a { color: var(--boing-accent-soft); }
